# Reflection on Writing an Agile Logbook

Writing an Agile Logbook throughout this project was an important part of tracking my progress, organizing my work, and reflecting on what I learned.

During September, the logbook helped me track my learning and preparation for the project. I recorded my progress in learning SQL queries, Transact-SQL (T-SQL), database administration, backup and recovery, performance monitoring, and query optimization.

## Benefits of the Agile Logbook

- Improved my time management and organization.
- Helped me identify challenges and risks.
- Allowed me to track completed tasks and plan future activities.
- Helped me evaluate my technical and personal growth.
- Encouraged continuous improvement and accountability.

## Conclusion

In conclusion, writing an Agile Logbook benefited me by improving my organization, time management, problem-solving skills, and ability to monitor my progress. It provided a clear record of my learning journey and the development of the SQL Server Health Dashboard.
